#: ../../guide/middlewares.rst:3
msgid "Middlewares"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/middlewares.rst:5
msgid "Middlewares wrap the handler call — the classic onion model. Use them for cross-cutting concerns: timing, database sessions, rate limiting, user throttling, context injection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/middlewares.rst:19
msgid "Inner vs outer middlewares"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/middlewares.rst:21
msgid "Every observer has **two** middleware chains:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/middlewares.rst:23
msgid "``observer.outer_middleware(...)`` — runs *before* filters are checked, on every single event of that observer. Use for context that filters themselves need (the built-in FSM middleware is outer for exactly this reason)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/middlewares.rst:27
msgid "``observer.middleware(...)`` — runs only for events that already matched a handler, immediately around the handler call. Cheaper; use for per-handler work like opening a DB session."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/middlewares.rst:37
msgid "Decorator and function-form middlewares"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/middlewares.rst:39
msgid "Besides classes, both managers accept plain async callables:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/middlewares.rst:51
msgid "BaseMiddleware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/middlewares.rst:53
msgid "`aiorubi.dispatcher.middlewares.base.BaseMiddleware`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/middlewares.rst:55
msgid "The base class for class-based middlewares. Subclass it and override ``__call__(handler, event, data)``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/middlewares.rst:58
msgid "``handler`` — the next step of the chain; always ``await handler(event, data)``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/middlewares.rst:59
msgid "``event`` — the event object for the observer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/middlewares.rst:60
msgid "``data`` — the context dict that will be given to filters and handlers; mutate it to inject dependencies:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/middlewares.rst:71
msgid "The ``data`` dict is exactly the context described in :doc:`handlers` — middleware entries become handler keyword arguments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/middlewares.rst:76
msgid "Skipping the rest of the chain"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/middlewares.rst:78
msgid "Raise :class:`~aiorubi.dispatcher.event.bases.CancelHandler` from a middleware to stop processing this update entirely; a plain ``return`` without calling ``handler`` also cuts the chain short."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/middlewares.rst:83
msgid "MiddlewareManager"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/middlewares.rst:85
msgid "`aiorubi.dispatcher.middlewares.manager.MiddlewareManager`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/middlewares.rst:87
msgid "Each observer carries two instances (``observer.middleware`` and ``observer.outer_middleware``). ``wrap_middlewares(managers, callback)`` builds the onion at dispatch time — you normally never touch it directly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/middlewares.rst:92
msgid "Built-in middlewares"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/middlewares.rst:94
msgid "The dispatcher installs three outer middlewares on the ``update`` observer (see :doc:`dispatcher`):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/middlewares.rst:97
msgid ":class:`~aiorubi.dispatcher.middlewares.error.ErrorsMiddleware` — converts handler exceptions into ``error``-observer events."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/middlewares.rst:99
msgid ":class:`~aiorubi.dispatcher.middlewares.user_context.UserContextMiddleware` — puts ``event_context`` (a frozen dataclass with ``chat_id`` and ``user_id``), plus the compatibility aliases ``event_from_user`` and ``event_chat``, into the data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/middlewares.rst:103
msgid ":class:`~aiorubi.fsm.middleware.FSMContextMiddleware` — FSM support; acquires the event-isolation lock and provides ``state`` / ``raw_state`` / ``fsm_storage``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/middlewares.rst:107
msgid "Scenes add one more outer middleware (``ScenesManager`` injection) when a :class:`~aiorubi.fsm.scene.SceneRegistry` is created — see :doc:`scenes`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/middlewares.rst:112
msgid "Propagation order"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/middlewares.rst:114
msgid "For a dispatch through routers ``dp → parent → child`` the observer's middlewares are collected **root first**: ``dp``'s outer middlewares run before ``parent``'s, which run before ``child``'s; the inner (per-handler) chain then wraps the winning handler. Filters and handlers always see the data as mutated by every middleware up to that point."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/middlewares.rst:121
msgid "Practical recipe — throttling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/middlewares.rst:142
msgid "Register it as *inner* middleware on a high-traffic observer so the check only costs anything for events that would run a handler anyway; as *outer* middleware it would also gate router-level filter checks."
msgstr ""

